# The core's own check, run by the `validate-core` [[cloud.job]] in
# ../trilogy.toml after the rollup and the enrichment table have landed.
#
# `validate datasource` reads the object and checks it against its declared
# grain, and fails the run when rows repeat: the rollup is declared at
# `tree_id`, and for months it carried 23,078 ids twice -- OSM nodes that two
# neighbouring cities both extracted -- with nothing anywhere reporting it,
# because each city's own parquet was clean and the duplication only existed
# in their union.  A refresh cannot notice that (it proves what it builds, not
# what it built), so this is a separate statement, on the same tick, ordered
# after both producers by the same derived edges the predictions job uses.
#
# Both inputs are reached through their `_source.preql` root views; this file
# imports no model and builds nothing.

import full_tree_info_source;
import tree_enrichment_source;

validate datasource full_tree_info;
validate datasource tree_enrichment;
